 "script": [
  "On 26 April 2026, a Sunday, the sun did what the market could not absorb: German solar peaked at 44.9 GW at 10:00 UTC. It was a weekend, so demand was lower.",
  "The day-ahead price was negative for 8 hours and fell to -€414/MWh. Generators were paying to be allowed to produce.",
  "For comparison, the weekdays before averaged €75/MWh. Wind averaged 5.4 GW across the day, against 44.9 GW of solar at its peak.",
  "Cheap hours like these are what flexible demand and batteries are for."
